<h3 class="pub-findings-header ">Annual and Monthly Price Changes</h3>
<p>Prices on average, as measured by the CPI, are 3.4% higher in July 2026 compared with July 2025.</p>
<p>The most notable changes in the year were increases in Education Services (+8.9%), Clothing &amp; Footwear (+8.5%), Housing, Water, Electricity, Gas &amp; Other Fuels (+7.7%) and Insurance &amp; Financial Services (+5.5%). No division recorded a decline when compared with July 2025.</p>
<p>Consumer Prices in July, as measured by the CPI, increased by 0.1% in the month. During July of last year prices also rose by 0.1% in the month. The most significant monthly price increases were in Recreation, Sport &amp; Culture (+2.7%) and Housing, Water, Electricity, Gas &amp; Other Fuels (+0.8%). The largest monthly decreases were in Clothing &amp; Footwear (-5.1%) and Transport (-0.9%).</p>
