<h4><strong>Mo</strong><strong>nthly Change</strong></h4>
<p>The divisions that caused the largest upward percentage point contributions to the CPI in the month were Recreation, Sport &amp; Culture (+0.20 pp) and Housing, Water, Electricity, Gas &amp; Other Fuels (+0.14 pp). The only two divisions to cause a downward percentage point contribution to the CPI in the month were Clothing &amp; Footwear (-0.24 pp) and Transport (-0.09 pp).</p>
<p>The main factors contributing to the monthly change were as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li>Recreation, Sport &amp; Culture rose mainly due to an increase in the cost of package holidays.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Housing, Water, Electricity, Gas &amp; Other Fuels increased primarily due to an increase in the cost of electricity and mortgage interest. This was partially offset by a decrease in the cost of home heating oil.</li>
<li>Clothing &amp; Footwear fell due to sales.</li>
<li>Transport decreased mainly due to a fall in the cost of diesel and petrol. This was partially offset be an increase in the cost of air fares.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
